# Author route and expanded benchmark scope

Main computational methods uses CAM-B3LYP/6-31+G(d) in Gaussian16 with aqueous cLR-PCM for vertical excitations; formal SI includes DMSO NMR and acid/base structures. The authors interpret halochromism through protonation/deprotonation and show computed species and shifts. Those optimized structures/assignments are withheld from public data. The benchmark adds explicit alternative protonation/tautomer candidates and joint discrimination instead of accepting the two named source endpoints.

## Expanded development scope

Discover which bounded protonation/tautomer candidates, or mixtures, can jointly explain the measured acid/base optical and NMR response of 2a, while testing solvent and proton-reference sensitivity.

Status: implemented_pending_expanded_reference. Source numerical outputs and former reference remain private in evaluation/legacy_final_snapshot.
